From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: select the registered external converter

License: GPL-2.0-only
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

Enca registers external converter programs under the converter name "extern".
The TeX regression requests the program name "recode" as though it were a
converter name. Select "extern" so the unchanged round-trip test uses the
configured GNU recode program. This also avoids routing TeX conversion through
librecode's in-process path, which aborts in free() on openEuler RISC-V even
though the separate librecode regression passes.

The option error was reproduced by run 31761326622 and the in-process abort by
exact-head run 32696957765. Remove the patch when upstream selects the external
converter for this TeX round trip.

---
 test/test-tex.sh | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/test-tex.sh b/test/test-tex.sh
--- a/test/test-tex.sh
+++ b/test/test-tex.sh
@@ -8,6 +8,6 @@ else
-  if $ENCA --list converters | grep '^librecode$' >/dev/null; then
+  if $ENCA --list converters | grep '^extern$' >/dev/null; then
     TEST_TEXT=$srcdir/cs-s.tex
-    OPTS="-L cs -C recode"
+    OPTS="-L cs -C extern"
     # File
     cp $TEST_TEXT $TESTNAME.actual
     $ENCA $OPTS -x UTF-8 $TESTNAME.actual || DIE=1
